  (text "FROM THE HAND-WRITTEN NETLIST THIS SHEET REPLACES (verbatim; the part notes are on each part's Note field):\n\nAUTHORITATIVE for connectivity. The drawing in power-entry.md is a representation of this file.\n\nSCOPE. That drawing shows the whole load switch - LT1641, R-ILIM, the timer and gate capacitors, the FB\ndivider and Q-LOADSW - so the export path can be read in one place. THOSE ARE module/umbilical-load-switch's\nPARTS and are declared `foreign:` here. This circuit owns the rail entry, the four bead-and-bulk branches and\nthe LM317.\n\n[J-PWR-EURO] THE HEADER'S SIXTEEN PINS, as the Doepfer bus numbers them: -12 V on the pair at pin 1 (the\nribbon's red stripe), GND on three pairs, +12 V, +5 V, then the bus CV and Gate, which this module does not\nuse [ds mechanical/DOEPFER-A100-BUS-CONNECTORS-a100b_e.gif]. Each supply is carried on both pins of its pair;\nCV and Gate are no-connects by decision.\n\n[of] qty 3: D1, D2, D3\n\n[of] qty 4: FB1..FB4\n\n[of] qty 4: C1..C4\n\n[NT-AGND-MOD] THE ANALOG STAR'S TIE. \"One origin, at the IDC's ground pin ... The analog return is its own\nregion joining at the star\" (power-entry.md, Grounding). A net tie is how a board joins two named nets at one\nplace and nowhere else, as NT-AGND does on the instrument's carrier. DIG_GND HAS NO TIE HERE: where it meets\nthe others is dig-gnd-topology, which is disputed.\n\n[PWR_EXPORT] The D2 branch. WHERE IT TERMINATES IS NOT DECIDABLE FROM THE DRAWING and is deliberately not\nasserted here - see the note at the foot of this file.\n\n[CV_13] The bus CV and Gate: a no-connect each, by decision.\n\nOPEN, AND NOT GUESSED AT.\n\n`BUS_POS12_RAW` is taken BEFORE D1/D2. Both Interfaces tables say so in the same words - power-entry.md:31\n\"The branch is taken **before** the diodes\" and umbilical-load-switch.md:18 \"Taken before the...\" - so two\nindependent statements agree and this file follows them.\n\nTHE DRAWING CANNOT BE READ THAT WAY WITH CONFIDENCE. It shows the D2 branch running into the load-switch\nblock, and the left-hand spine is the connector body rather than a rail, so the two readings are not\ndistinguishable from the ASCII. That is the whole argument for this file existing: A PICTURE CAN BE AMBIGUOUS\nAND A NETLIST CANNOT.\n\nSo the D2 branch's far end is left unasserted. It is one of: - the exported rail's reverse protection, with\nthe load switch upstream on the raw bus, which is what both tables describe; or - in series with the load\nswitch output, which is what the drawing looks like and which would give the exported rail protection the\ntables do not credit it with. The difference is what reverse-polarity protection the instrument actually has.\nResolve it on the page, then state it here - do not resolve it here from a reading of the picture.\n\nThe load switch's own parts (R-ILIM, the timer and gate network, the FB divider) are `foreign:` above so the\ndrawing checks, and are NOT netted here: a part belongs to one circuit's netlist, or two files can disagree\nabout one connection and both look right." (at 408.94 38.099999999999994 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 2e80c672-fb66-511c-8f18-a2cc1dcf218e))
  (text "PARTS THIS PAGE'S DRAWING SHOWS AND THIS CIRCUIT DOES NOT OWN - netlist.yaml `foreign:`, exported from the FOREIGN lines below.\nEach is counted, netted and ordered by its owner; declaring it keeps the drawing checkable (tools/check-netlist.py).\nFOREIGN R-ILIM: owner module/umbilical-load-switch, row R-ILIM\nFOREIGN R-GATE-SER: owner module/umbilical-load-switch, row R-GATE-SER\nFOREIGN R-GATE-COMP: owner module/umbilical-load-switch, row R-GATE-COMP\nFOREIGN C-TIMER: owner module/umbilical-load-switch, row C-TIMER-LOADSW\nFOREIGN C-GATE: owner module/umbilical-load-switch, row C-GATE-LOADSW\nFOREIGN R-FB-HI: owner module/umbilical-load-switch, row R-FB-HI\nFOREIGN R-FB-LO: owner module/umbilical-load-switch, row R-FB-LO" (at 40.64 17.78 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 5b48fe4f-10cc-5714-8615-d7de8e8c7db6))
  (sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1")))
)
